WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.894
OpenAI publishes its

00:00:01.706 --> 00:00:02.897
internal perplexity

00:00:02.708 --> 00:00:03.321
curve

00:00:03.846 --> 00:00:05.485
OpenAI chief scientist

00:00:05.296 --> 00:00:06.829
Jakub Pachocki argues

00:00:06.641 --> 00:00:08.232
that pretraining perplexity

00:00:08.268 --> 00:00:09.034
should become a

00:00:08.846 --> 00:00:10.473
shared cross-lab metric

00:00:10.296 --> 00:00:11.345
for tracking AI

00:00:11.157 --> 00:00:12.537
progress and setting

00:00:12.348 --> 00:00:13.338
safety limits

00:00:13.469 --> 00:00:15.072
and discloses OpenAI's

00:00:14.884 --> 00:00:16.039
own log-perplexity

00:00:15.851 --> 00:00:16.593
figures

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:18.548
Pachocki frames modern

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.668
AI as training

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.341
a compressor

00:00:20.483 --> 00:00:21.508
and says held-out

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.145
perplexity

00:00:22.263 --> 00:00:23.430
has been OpenAI's

00:00:23.242 --> 00:00:24.326
constant measure of

00:00:24.138 --> 00:00:24.940
progress

00:00:25.478 --> 00:00:26.338
On its current

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.470
main evaluation set

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:28.886
GPT-3 .

00:00:28.697 --> 00:00:29.605
5 sat at

00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:30.690
a log-perplexity of

00:00:30.502 --> 00:00:32.588
about 0.99 and

00:00:32.436 --> 00:00:34.145
GPT-4 at about

00:00:33.957 --> 00:00:36.866
0.91 below 0.8

00:00:36.678 --> 00:00:37.656
the company saw

00:00:37.468 --> 00:00:39.272
transformative capabilities

00:00:39.119 --> 00:00:40.781
in cybersecurity and

00:00:40.605 --> 00:00:41.583
mathematics

00:00:42.102 --> 00:00:43.116
Full story on

00:00:42.927 --> 00:00:43.823
the dashboard
